{"kind":"remark","label":"rem:atomic-valence-open-sites-remark","title":"Valences of H, C, N, O and lone-pair assignment","html":"<a id=\"rem:atomic-valence-open-sites-remark\"></a><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"left\">Atom</th>\n<th align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z</code></th>\n<th align=\"left\">Config</th>\n<th align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v(Z)</code></th>\n<th align=\"left\">Open sites</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\">H</td>\n<td align=\"left\">1</td>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1s^1</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">1</td>\n<td align=\"left\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\">C</td>\n<td align=\"left\">6</td>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[He]\\,2s^2 2p^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">4</td>\n<td align=\"left\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\">N</td>\n<td align=\"left\">7</td>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[He]\\,2s^2 2p^3</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">3</td>\n<td align=\"left\">3 (+1 lone pair)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\">O</td>\n<td align=\"left\">8</td>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[He]\\,2s^2 2p^4</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">2</td>\n<td align=\"left\">2 (+2 lone pairs)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The LP dual assigns electrons to bonding versus lone-pair positions by comparing the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_1</code> cost of sharing versus retaining.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/atomic-valence-open-sites-remark.md","heading":"Remark","number":"18.3.4","page":"b/rem-atomic-valence-open-sites-remark"}
